 process \"escapes the kill\", but not that git-gud will hang waiting for it. `--timeout` exists to bound the run, so this undercuts it.\n- **Fix:** on timeout, and in the 2-second fallback after the reviewer exits, call `child.stdout.destroy()`, `child.stderr.destroy()` and `child.unref()`. Or end the process explicitly once the results are printed.\n\n### Checked and fine\n- **Sandbox with `--timeout` (verified):** bwrap runs with `--new-session`, so the agent inside does leave the group. It still dies, though, because of `--die-with-parent` and `--unshare-pid`. The run with `--sandbox --timeout=0.03` finished in 3 s and left no `sleep` processes.\n- **Workspace cleanup on a signal (verified):** the workspace is deleted before the reviewer groups are killed. Over five SIGTERM runs, with a reviewer writing files the whole time, no workspace was left behind.\n- **By reading:** the one-pass `cleanText`, how `--evidence-stage` is validated and routed, the `--timeout` bounds (a week is well under the timer's limit), and the honesty-stage separator test all look right.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
